INT. ABANDONED LIGHTHOUSE KEEPER'S QUARTERS - NIGHT

A round room. Peeling wallpaper the color of old tea. A cast-iron stove. A spiral stair winding up into darkness. Salt crusts the windows.

Five friends have made camp on the floor with sleeping bags and flashlights.

HARPER OSEI-LINDQVIST (20s, canvas jacket, mug of instant coffee) sits cross-legged near the stove.

JASPER "JAZ" ABERNATHY-TRAN (20s, knit cap, deck of cards) shuffles with a nervous flick.

KEZIAH ONYANGO-FALLOWS (20s, vintage windbreaker, hair in a bandana) reads a tattered logbook by flashlight.

MATEUSZ "MATT" KOWALSKI-BELLO (30s, flannel, camera tripod) adjusts a lens.

And LOTTIE SUNDARAM-REEVES (20s, oversized sweater, pale), who hasn't spoken since they arrived, hugs her knees by the window.

HARPER
So the logbook. Read it again.

KEZIAH
"October ninth. Fog thick as wool. The light turns but no ship answers. I hear footsteps on the stair, though I am alone."

JAZ
Spooky.

KEZIAH
"October tenth. The footsteps again. This time they stop at my door."

MATT
Cut it. We can't use this on camera.

JAZ
Why not?

MATT
It's too good. We'll need to reshoot.

HARPER
It's a log, Matt. It's not a script.

KEZIAH
"October eleventh. The door is open. I did not open it."

A creak from the stair above. Everyone looks. Nothing. Only the dark.

LOTTIE
(very quietly)
There's something on the stairs.

HARPER
There's nothing.

LOTTIE
There's something.

MATT
Where?

LOTTIE
The third landing.

Keziah clicks her flashlight toward the third landing. The beam finds a pale shape, slim and still, standing with its head tilted. A figure in a keeper's coat, face blurred as if seen through wet glass.

KEZIAH
Oh no.

JAZ
Don't move. Nobody move.

HARPER
(through her teeth)
Matt, are you filming?

MATT
Yes.

HARPER
Keep filming.

The figure takes one step down. The boards creak. Another. Jaz drops the cards; they scatter like white birds. Matt swings the camera. Lottie rises, steps toward the stair, mesmerized.

KEZIAH
Lottie, don't.

LOTTIE
It wants to show me something.

HARPER
Lottie!

She grabs Lottie's arm. Lottie turns, eyes glassy, smiling.

LOTTIE
(softly)
He's lonely.

The figure reaches the second landing. The temperature drops. Their breath fogs. The stove flame bends sideways, then goes out.

Darkness. Five flashlights jitter. Five beams find the keeper's coat, now at the bottom of the stair, its face almost clear. Almost human.

KEEPER
(a whisper, a wind)
Stay.

Jaz screams. Matt backs into the stove. Keziah slams the logbook shut. Harper wrenches Lottie back with both hands, and the five of them stumble toward the door. They crash through it, tumbling onto the wet grass outside. The sea roars. The lighthouse beam sweeps over them, steady, impossible, from a lamp that has been dead for forty years.

They stare up. The beam swings away.

Lottie, panting, laughs weakly.

LOTTIE (CONT'D)
Nobody believed me.

MATT
(shaking)
I got it. I got all of it.

HARPER
Delete it.

MATT
What?

HARPER
Delete it. Please.

Matt looks at the camera. At Harper. At the lighthouse. He nods. Presses the button, and the light on the camera goes out.
